export anchor MarketDepthStyle:
    number: 367
    screen: FinanceBudget
    name: Market depth
    idea: The budget read as an order book, each category a mirrored depth row with spent growing left and remaining growing right from a central limit column, balances on a ticker strip, savings as a goal ladder and transactions as a trade tape.
    base: dark
    palette:
        floor: #090c12, the page and the style sheet
        panel: #0f131b, the three desk panels, fields and rows
        head: #151b26, panel title bars, the ticker strip and the limit column
        grid: #232b3a, 1px gaps between panels and every row line
        ink: #dfe6f2, text and figures
        muted: #93a0b5, column heads, dates and side labels
        spent: #f2b45c, spent figures and spent depth bars
        remaining: #5fcbe3, remaining figures and bars, the primary button and focus
        over: #ff8593, deficit hatching, the OVER tag and the owed balance
        in: #7fe3a9, money in on the tape and filled goal levels
    type:
        One monospace stack, ui-monospace, JetBrains Mono, SF Mono, Menlo,
        Consolas, Liberation Mono. Base 13px. Position figures are 18px at 700,
        ticker figures 15px at 700, depth figures 14px at 700 in their side
        colour, panel heads 11px caps tracked .12em at 700.
    layout:
        A full width trading desk. The top strip holds a BW slash MONEY mark, a
        ticker of cells for Everyday, Savings, Credit card with a clock and DUE
        12 NOV in red, and Oct budget left 60, then MARA OKAFOR, EUR, OCT on the
        right. Below, three panels sit edge to edge with 1px grid gaps, 260px,
        flexible and 330px. The left panel lists Positions and then a Goal
        ladder for the Japan trip, ten stacked levels of 500 from 500 at the
        bottom to 5,000 at the top, six filled green and the seventh two fifths,
        with 3,200 of 5,000 filled and the target under it. The centre panel is
        Budget depth with a header reading spent, limit, remaining. Each
        category is a 52px row with a framed central cell holding the name in
        caps and its limit. To the left an amber translucent bar grows from the
        centre to the share of the limit spent, with the spent figure on its
        end. To the right a cyan bar grows by the share remaining. Rent shows 0
        and a dashed FILLED box. Eating out has a dotted red cap on the spent
        side and a red hatched deficit bar with minus 62 and a boxed OVER tag. A
        spread row shows 1,870 spent, 1,930 total and 60 left, then a key. The
        right panel is the Tape with date, payee, an IN or OUT word with an
        arrow, and amount. Below 1100px the tape drops under, below 760px all
        stack with the book first.
    spacing: A 4px unit. 8 to 12px cell padding, 52px depth rows and 1px gaps between panels.
    density:
        High. Three panels, a ticker, a five row book with totals, a ten level
        ladder and a tape.
    corners: Square, 2px on buttons and fields only.
    borders:
        1px grid lines everywhere, panels split by 1px gaps, and a framed limit
        column in the middle of the book.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Tiny glyphs beside capital words. A triangle with OVER in a solid box, a
        ruled square with FILLED in a dashed box, arrows with IN and OUT and a
        clock for due.
    focus: A 2px cyan inset outline with a faint cyan inner wash.
    tone:
        Terse trading labels in capitals, such as Positions, Budget depth, Tape,
        OVER, FILLED and 60 left.
